│ patch_description        │ The key insight is that CZ-RY-CZ creates non-trivial multi-body correlations that a       │
│                          │ single CZ round cannot produce. With shared parameters, we get strong regularization (low │
│                          │ generalization gap) while the doubled entanglement depth significantly increases          │
│                          │ expressiveness.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Structure per block:                                                                      │
│                          │ 1. Shared RY input (1 param) — non-diagonal mixer                                         │
│                          │ 2. Shared RZ phase (1 param) — phase fine-tuning                                          │
│                          │ 3. Full hypercube CZ (12 edges, 0 params) — entanglement round 1                          │
│                          │ 4. Shared RY mid (1 param) — mid-circuit mixer creates interference                       │
│                          │ 5. Full hypercube CZ (12 edges, 0 params) — entanglement round 2                          │
│                          │ 6. Shared RY out + Shared RX out (2 params) — output measurement preparation              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Total: 5 params × 6 blocks = 30 circuit + 2 readout = 32 params.                          │
│                          │ This is only 6 more than the best design but with dramatically richer entanglement        │
│                          │ structure.                                                                                │
